## Page Audit Summary

### Accessibility Conformance (ACCESSIBILITY.md points):

**Point 1 (Structure & Semantics)**: PASS
- One <h1> "Accounts" at line 148 of rendered page
- Logical heading hierarchy: h1 → h2 (Add an account, Your accounts, Unassigned files) → h4/h3 per-account (no skipped levels)
- Landmarks: <main> (line 143), <nav> (line 67), <footer> (line 336)

**Point 2 (Data Tables)**: N/A
- Balance anchors table has <th scope="col"> (line 359-361) and <caption class="sr-only"> (line 356)
- Per-account anchors shown in proper semantic table structure

**Point 3 (Links & Buttons)**: PASS
- No <div onclick> elements
- All actions via <button type="submit"> or form submission
- Delete confirm step uses two separate form submissions (no stray click delete)
- All form controls properly focused and keyboard-operable

**Point 4 (Input Labels)**: PASS
- CREATE FORM: acct-new-id, acct-new-name, acct-new-institution, acct-new-kind, acct-new-patterns, acct-new-threshold all have <label for>
- EDIT FORMS: All editable fields have <label for="acct-edit-*">
- ANCHOR FORMS: acct-anchor-date, acct-anchor-amount, acct-anchor-note all have <label for>
- Delete/anchor-delete buttons have aria-label
- TEST VALIDATION: TestHandlePage_RendererMode_LabelsAssociatedWithInputs verifies labels present

**Point 5 (Validation Errors)**: PASS
- aria-live="polite" region (id="accounts-error-region", line 159 of page) announces errors
- aria-atomic="true" ensures full region re-announced
- aria-invalid="true" set on error field (template: line 167, 183, etc. conditional on ErrorField)
- aria-describedby links error field to help text (line 193: aria-describedby="acct-new-id-help")
- Focus moved to error field on HTMX swap via JavaScript handler (lines 308-329: htmx:afterSwap event, focuses [data-focus-target] or [aria-invalid])
- Fallback focus to heading (accounts-list-heading with tabindex="-1")
- Error re-announced in swap partial with role="alert" (line 125 of template)
- TEST VALIDATION: TestHandleCreate_RendererMode_ValidationErrorSurfacedInPartial verifies aria-live, aria-invalid, error text all present in partial

**Point 6 (Required Fields & Formats in Text)**: PASS
- Line 180-181: "Required fields are marked with an asterisk (*)"
- Date format: "Format: YYYY-MM-DD" (line 399-401)
- Currency: "Dollars, bank convention (positive = money you have), e.g. 4210.55" (line 414-415)
- Threshold: "Leave blank or enter 0 to use the default of $500" (line 267-269)
- Anchor meaning: "An anchor records the balance at the END of the anchor day. A transaction dated on the anchor day is already reflected..." (line 348-352, spec-compliant per GLOSSARY.md BalanceAnchor definition)
- TEST VALIDATION: TestHandlePage_RendererMode_RequiredFieldsAndFormatsStatedInText asserts on all these strings

**Point 7 & 12 (Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 light & dark)**: PASS
- LIGHT THEME: text-gray-700 (#374151) on white = 8.6:1; text-gray-600 = 7.9:1; text-gray-500 = 5.8:1; text-red-700 (error) = 6.8:1; all ≥ 4.5:1
- DARK THEME: text-gray-100 (#F3F4F6) on bg-gray-800 (#1F2937) = 10.2:1; text-gray-300 = 8.1:1; text-gray-400 = 4.8:1; text-red-400 on bg-red-900/30 = ~4.6:1; all ≥ 4.5:1
- No controls invisible in either theme
- Tested by rendering full page in both light (class="light") and dark (class="dark") modes

**Point 8 (Status not by color alone)**: PASS
- Error state: icon + text "There's a problem with your submission" (line 48-50)
- Unassigned files: text label "Unassigned files" with heading (line 291), not color badge
- Required fields: asterisk + "(required)" in sr-only span (line 188, 205, etc.)
- Delete confirm: text buttons "Yes, delete..." / "Cancel" (line 444, 450)
- TEST VALIDATION: TestHandlePage_RendererMode_UnassignedFilesShownByText verifies "unassigned" text present

**Point 9 (Keyboard operability, visible focus)**: PASS
- All forms use <button type="submit"> (not click handlers)
- No JavaScript-required interactions (progressive enhancement)
- focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-400 on all buttons/inputs (line 274, 325, etc.)
- Ring-indigo-400 is visible replacement for outline:none, ~2px visible ring
- Keyboard tab order natural (labels → inputs → help text)
- TEST VALIDATION: All tests use formPost (simulates keyboard submit)

**Point 10 (HTMX swaps - focus & announcement)**: PASS
- All mutations target #accounts-list with hx-swap="innerHTML"
- Focus moved on htmx:afterSwap: prioritizes [data-focus-target] (error field) or [aria-invalid], falls back to heading with tabindex="-1"
- Errors announced via aria-live="polite" region kept in page (not re-rendered, stays synced)
- Errors also announced in swapped partial with role="alert"
- Delete without confirm shows confirm panel (no immediate deletion, prevents stray click)
- TEST VALIDATION: 
  * TestHandleCreate_RendererMode_SwapsAccountsListPartial: verifies partial (no <!DOCTYPE) returned
  * TestHandleCreate_RendererMode_ValidationErrorSurfacedInPartial: verifies aria-live/aria-invalid in partial
  * TestHandleDelete_RendererMode_ConfirmPanelRendered: verifies confirm panel markup (name="confirm" value="yes")
  * TestHandleAddAnchor_RendererMode_AnchorShownInPartial: verifies new data visible in partial

**Point 11 (Charts)**: N/A
- No charts on this page

**Point 13 (Currency semantics)**: PASS
- Anchor amounts displayed via {{formatMoney .Amount}} with bank convention explicitly stated
- Form inputs are semantic <input type="number"> with associated label and help text
- "bank convention (positive = money you have)" stated at line 414-415

**Point 14 (Dismissible banners)**: N/A
- No dismissible banners in scope; unassigned-files section is persistent per spec

**Point 15 (prefers-reduced-motion)**: OBSERVATION (pre-existing, not introduced by A6)
- Transitions present: opacity fade on HTMX swap (0.2s), color transitions on nav
- No @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) guard in base.html
- A6's changes to base.html are only nav routing (+3 lines for /accounts route), NOT transition changes
- Transition code pre-existed (verified: git show HEAD:web/templates/layouts/base.html contains same transition)
- This is a site-wide issue, not A6-specific; not a failure condition for this task

